<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">Notes to Standalone and Consolidated Unaudited Financial Results for the quarter and six months ended September 30, 2019:  n  n1.tThe Audit Committee has reviewed the above results and the Board of Directors has approved the above results and its release at their respective meetings held on November 14, 2019. The Statutory Auditors of the Company have carried out a limited review of these results.  n  n2.tBased on the information reviewed by the Chief Operating Decision Maker (CODM), the Company has single operating segment, being integrated post-production services.  n  n3.tPursuant to the shareholders’ approval, a business transfer agreement (the “BTA”) has been executed subsequent to the period end, between Prime Focus Limited (the “Company”) and DNEG Creative Services Limited, a subsidiary of the Company (“DNEG”), for sale of the Company’s VFX business on a slump sale basis, for a consideration of Rs. 27,000 lakhs, subject to closing conditions as specified in the BTA.  n  n4.tSome of Indian subsidiaries of the Group have elected to exercise the option permitted under section 115BAA of the Income Tax Act, 1961 as introduced by the Taxation Laws (Amendment) Ordinance, 2019. Consequently, remeasurement of deferred tax assets and liability position of such companies’ basis the rate prescribed under the aforesaid section, has resulted in recognition of net reversal of deferred tax expense of Rs. 2,235 lakhs for the six months ended September 30, 2019.  n  n5.tThe Group has adopted Ind AS 116 on “Leases” with the date of initial application being April 1, 2019. Ind AS 116 replaces Ind AS 17 on “Leases” and related interpretation and guidance. The Group has applied Ind AS 116 using modified retrospective approach, under which the cumulative effect of initial application is recognised in retained earnings as at April 1, 2019. As a result, the comparative information has not been restated.   n  nOn transition to Ind AS 116, the Group recognised right-to-use assets amounting to Rs 57,230.82 lakhs   n[Rs 2,881.54 lakhs], lease liability amounting to Rs 61,169.81 lakhs [Rs 2,992.74 lakhs] and   nRs 2,831.64 lakhs (debit) [Rs 111.20 lakhs (debit)] in retained earnings as at April 1, 2019. The Company has discounted lease payments using the applicable incremental borrowing rate as at April 1, 2019 for measuring the lease liability.   n  nDuring the quarter and six months ended September 30, 2019, the Company has recognised interest expense on lease liabilities amounting to Rs 907.91 lakhs [Rs 86.04 lakhs] and Rs 1,812.09 lakhs   n[Rs 171.92 lakhs] respectively and depreciation on right-of-use assets amounting to Rs 1,590.51 lakhs [Rs 156.57 lakhs] and Rs 3,228.35 lakhs [Rs 299.83 lakhs] respectively. Consequently, rental expenses are lower by Rs 2,133.42 lakhs [Rs 175.67 lakhs] and Rs 4,368.56 lakhs [Rs 350.87 lakhs] respectively.  n  n* figures in brackets are pertaining to standalone financial results of the Company.   n  n6.tThe standalone and consolidated statement of cash flows for the six months ended September 30, 2018 as reported in these financial results have been approved by the Company’s Board of Directors, but have not been subjected to review by the auditors.  n  n7.tPrevious period figures have been regrouped and re-arranged wherever necessary to correspond to the figures of the current period.  n  n  n  nFor and on behalf of the Board of Directors  nttttt  ntttttttNaresh Malhotra  n                                                                                                                                                          Director  nDIN No. 00004597  nPlace: Mumbai    nDate: November 14, 2019</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
